{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_18_195236522#3_218548923","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a dedicated Minimalism visual arts article with direct origin evidence: European roots in geometric abstraction, De Stijl, Constructivism and Brâncuși, inspiration from specific artists, and emergence as a reaction against Abstract Expressionism in New York in the early 1960s. It directly supports an answer to whether Minimalism 'comes from creativity' by identifying its art-historical sources.","learned":"Minimalism in visual art emerged in New York in the early 1960s, with roots in geometric abstraction, De Stijl, Constructivism, Brâncuși, and as a reaction against Abstract Expressionism."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2401","reason":"This query produced highly relevant art-history origin evidence; continue through its ranked results to find more grade-3 sources."}}
