{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ minimalism \"originated\" \"new york\" \"1960s\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_462713867#0_1009643441","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2405","rank":1,"snippet":"Minimalist music is derived from Minimalist Visual Arts and is associated with reduced or minimal music. Home / Uncategorized / Characteristics of Minimalist Music Minimalist music is derived from Minimalist Visual Arts and is associated with reduced or minimal music. Minimalist music is austere with static harmony, pulse-driven, diatonic and a static instrumentation style. This music has been used in various Hollywood movies, like ‘Minority Report’ ‘Traffic’ and ‘Solaris’ as their soundtrack and background scores. History of Minimalist Music This music came about as a reaction against other music styles, mainly Serialism. This music style was <cover>originated in the late 1960s, in New York downtown. Minimalism </cover>was pioneered by a group of American composers, Michael Nyman and Tom Johnson. Initially it was looked up as a form of experimental music called the New York Hypnotic School and was later recognized as a popular experimental music style. This music style was inspired from the minimalist art forms. Would you like to write for us?\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"Characteristics of Minimalist Music - Melodyful\" , \"url\": \"https://melodyful.com/characteristics-of-minimalist-music\" }"}}
