{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_430904731#2_383672660","relevance":0,"reason":"The passage is about Pop Art origins and only mentions Minimalism as another movement; it does not explain Minimalism's origin or whether it comes from creativity.","learned":"The phrase 'origins art movement' can still retrieve adjacent art movements unless Minimalism is constrained more tightly."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"minimalism\" \"emerged in new york\" \"early 1960s\")","reason":"Use a distinctive origin phrase from the strong evidence to find additional dedicated Minimalism sources and avoid broad adjacent art-movement pages."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"minimalism\" \"emerged in new york\" \"early 1960s\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_09_1196858521#3_2099638835","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2408","rank":1,"snippet":"Serra Do Not Miss Post-Minimalism Light and Space American Art Important Art and Artists of Minimalism Die Fahne Hoch! (1959) Die (1962) Lever (1966) Useful Resources on Minimalism Books Share \" , \"segment\": \"And I like using those different levels.\\\" 6 of 9 \\\"No to transcendence and spiritual values, heroic scale, anguished decisions, historicizing narrative, valuable artifact, intelligent structure, interesting visual experience.\\\" 7 of 9 \\\"The steel and the space, or the object and the void, become one and the same.\\\" 8 of 9 \\\"I like art as thought better than art as work. I've always maintained this. It's important to me that I don't get my hands dirty. It's not because I'm instinctively lazy. It's a declaration: art is thought.\\\" 9 of 9 Summary of Minimalism<cover>Minimalism emerged in New York in the early 1960s </cover>among artists who were self-consciously renouncing recent art they thought had become stale and academic.\" , \"start_char\": 1241.000000 , \"title\": \"Minimalism Movement Overview | TheArtStory\" , \"url\": \"http://www.theartstory.org/movement-minimalism.htm\" }"}}
