{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"minimalist music\" \"reaction against\" \"serialism\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_1796760965#1_3095160229","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2438","rank":2,"snippet":"In 1945 Ginastera moved to the United States where he had the opportunity to study with the well known American composer Aaron Copland Serialism is a compositional technique in which a series of rhythms, dynamics, or tone colors could serve as a unifying idea Twelve-tone compositional techniques used to organize rhythm, dynamics, tone color, and other dimensions of music to produce totally controlled and organized music are called serialism In chance, or aleatory music the composer chooses pitches, tone colors, and rhythms by random methods Minimalism as an artistic movement was a<cover>reaction against the complexity of serialism and the randomness of chance music Minimalist music </cover>is characterized by the development of musical materials through random methods Since 1950 many composers have returned to electronic music Around 1940, John Cage invented the prepared piano, a (n) grand piano whose sound is altered by objects such as bolts, screws, rubber bands, pieces of felt, paper, and plastic inserted between the strings of some of the keys Edgard Varese's Poeme electronique was designed for the 1958 Brussels World Fair;\" , \"start_char\": 1349.000000 , \"title\": \"Test 6/26/12 ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_462713867#0_1009643441","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
