{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"minimalist design\" \"de stijl\" \"bauhaus\" \"japanese\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_1341996649#6_2742977908","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2442","rank":3,"snippet":"Why Less Is More Where Did the <cover>Minimalist Design Trend Come From? Minimalism’s Connections to Other Influential Design Movements 60 Minimalist Logos by vuuuds in Templates Axon | Minimalist Sans Serif Family by Graphicfresh in Fonts Minimalist Business Card by Propex in Templates Characteristics of Minimalism Web Design Flat Design Google’s Material Design Minimal Wordpress Theme- Simply Pro by Bloom Blog Shop in Web Themes Minimalist Interior Design Surfaces Neutral or Light Color Bases Consistent Textures and Tones Minimalist Architecture The Bare Essentials A Respect for Space Japanese Architecture Beauty in Simplicity Products Seen In This Post: Free lettering worksheets Getting started with hand lettering? Marc Schenker \" , \"segment\": \"In the case of minimalism, its European origins are found in the geometric-abstraction creations of painters who were associated with the Bauhaus movement. One of the mottos of Bauhaus was the famous line, form follows function, which stresses that any design should put a priority on usability and any aesthetic considerations should come in second. Painters such as Piet Mondrian and Kazimir Malevich are standout examples, as well as artists who were associated with the De Stijl </cover>movement (which translates to “The Style”), a ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_43802617#1_112501278","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_43802617#2_112503978","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
